{"assets":[],"contentKind":"statement","contestId":"2022","diagnostics":[],"document":{"children":[{"attrs":{"level":1,"role":"title"},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"A. Bus to Pénjamo"}],"kind":"heading"},{"attrs":{"role":"time_limit"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"time limit per test"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"1 second"}],"kind":"container"},{"attrs":{"role":"memory_limit"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"memory limit per test"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"256 megabytes"}],"kind":"container"},{"attrs":{"role":"body"},"children":[{"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Ya vamos llegando a Péeeenjamoo ♫♫♫ "}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"container"}],"kind":"container"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"There are $$$n$$$ families travelling to Pénjamo to witness Mexico's largest-ever \"walking a chicken on a leash\" marathon. The $$$i$$$-th family has $$$a_i$$$ family members. All families will travel using a single bus consisting of $$$r$$$ rows with $$$2$$$ seats each."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"A person is considered "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"happy"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" if: "}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"attrs":{"ordered":false},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" Another family member is seated in the same row as them, or "}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" They are sitting alone in their row (with an empty seat next to them). "}],"kind":"list_item"}],"kind":"list"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Determine the maximum number of happy people in an optimal seating arrangement. Note that "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"everyone"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" must be seated in the bus."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"It is guaranteed that all family members will fit on the bus. Formally, it is guaranteed that $$$\\displaystyle\\sum_{i=1}^{n}a_i \\le 2r$$$."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"input_specification"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Each test contains multiple test cases. The first line contains the number of test cases $$$t$$$ ($$$1 \\le t \\le 1000$$$). The description of the test cases follows."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The first line of each test case contains two integers $$$n$$$ and $$$r$$$ ($$$1 \\le n \\le 100$$$; $$$1 \\le r \\le 500$$$) — the number of families and the number of rows in the bus."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The second line contains $$$n$$$ integers $$$a_1, a_2, \\ldots, a_n$$$ ($$$1 \\le a_i \\le 10$$$) — the number of family members in each family."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"output_specification"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"For each test case, output the maximum number of happy people in an optimal seating arrangement."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"samples"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Example"}],"kind":"heading"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample"},"children":[{"attrs":{"role":"sample_input"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"\n4\n3 3\n2 3 1\n3 3\n2 2 2\n4 5\n1 1 2 2\n4 5\n3 1 1 3\n"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample_output"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"\n4\n6\n6\n6\n"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"note"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Note"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"